  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "We have RNA-seq, proteomics and DNA methylation for the same 50 glioma samples. Would DRAGON or LIONESS-DRAGON give me a single partial-correlation network that connects all three layers at once?"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"Would DRAGON or LIONESS-DRAGON give me a single partial-correlation network that connects all three layers at once?\" -- I couldn't match this to anything a registered NetZoo workflow produces or lets you set. DRAGON gives: one undirected partial-correlation network within and between two matched omics layers (any two, e.g. expression and methylation), across all samples. A p-value and a Benjamini-Hochberg adjusted p-value for every edge (adjusted within each layer and across the layers), to filter edges by significance. LIONESS-DRAGON gives: one two-layer partial-correlation network per sample, plus the aggregate.\n\nI couldn't match this to a result any registered NetZoo workflow produces, so none is offered.\n\nRegistered workflows that take the kind of data you described: PANDA, PUMA, LIONESS-PANDA, LIONESS-PUMA, LIONESS-COEXPRESSION, COBRA, DRAGON, LIONESS-DRAGON, OTTER, GIRAFFE, BONOBO. Tell me if one of them gives what you meant, or which result you need.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
